      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I made a mistake. LLVM actually supports the attribute for loong64, but it does not automatically define the __loongarch_asx macro compared to the \"-mlasx\" flag. The intrinsic declaration in the header file (lasxintrin.h) is wrapped by __loongarch_asx macro, which causes undeclared compile error. We have already fixed this usage and all tests passed. Please review this change again, thanks.",
